  "title": "Suffolk Wildfire Near Sizewell B Sparks Major Emergency as Hundreds Evacuated",
  "summary": "The dramatic wildfire that swept across the Suffolk coast has become one of the most significant environmental emergencies in the United Kingdom this summer. Covering more than 80 hectares of land near the Sizewell B nuclear power station, the blaze forced hundreds of residents and holidaymakers to evacuate while firefighters battled difficult weather conditions to contain the flames. The incident highlights the growing threat of wildfires across the UK as prolonged drought, repeated heatwaves,",
